---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About Gesture Synth School | Gesture Synth Practice"
	description="Gesture Synth School is a free practice companion for Gesture Synth: chord charts, hand gesture guides, and a webcam play-along songbook."
	canonical="https://gesturesynthschool.com/about/"
	ogType="article"
	jsonLd={[
		{
			'@context': 'https://schema.org',
			'@type': 'AboutPage',
			name: 'About Gesture Synth School',
			url: 'https://gesturesynthschool.com/about/',
			mainEntity: {
				'@type': 'WebSite',
				name: 'Gesture Synth School',
				url: 'https://gesturesynthschool.com/',
			},
		},
	]}
>
	<article class="content container">
		<p class="eyebrow">About</p>
		<h1>About Gesture Synth School</h1>
		<p class="lede">
			Gesture Synth School is a free, independent practice companion for Gesture Synth —
			the webcam instrument that turns your hands into a chord machine.
		</p>

		<h2>What this site does</h2>
		<p>
			Gesture Synth maps hand gestures to music: your left hand picks a scale degree and a
			major or minor key, your right hand shapes the chord quality and octave. It is magical
			the first time the song rings out — and it is hard to know where to start.
		</p>
		<p>
			This site fills that gap. The songbook turns popular songs into chord charts written
			in gesture language, and the play-along player scores your hands against each target
			shape with a backing pad and metronome. The
			<a href="/guide/">how to play guide</a> and
			<a href="/chords/">chord reference</a> document every gesture against the open-source
			engine, and the <a href="/weld/">Gesture Synth Weld guide</a> covers the popular web
			version of the instrument.
		</p>

		<h2>Why it exists</h2>
		<p>
			Gesture Synth went viral on short video, and thousands of people are learning it from
			clips — but clips move fast and practice needs structure. We built the songbook as a
			place to slow down: pick a song, learn the shapes, and build the muscle memory one
			chord at a time.
		</p>

		<h2>Privacy</h2>
		<p>
			The practice tools run entirely in your browser. Your webcam is never uploaded or
			stored by us — hand tracking happens locally on your device. For the full details, see
			the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Contact</h2>
		<p>
			Found a broken chart, have a song request, or want to report an issue? We would love
			to hear from you at
			<a href="mailto:feedback@gesturesynthschool.com"
				>feedback@gesturesynthschool.com</a
			>.
		</p>

		<div class="card cta">
			<h3>Ready to play?</h3>
			<p class="muted">Start with the beginner songs and work your way up.</p>
			<a class="btn" href="/">Browse the songbook</a>
			<a class="btn" href="/guide/">Learn the gestures</a>
		</div>
	</article>
</Layout>
